# PyInstaller
#  Usually these files are written by a parent script to a temporary
#  directory. In the case where you want to deploy the binary files
#  alongside your code, you can use PyInstaller to create a

#  single file executable instead of a folder with many files.
#  In this case, you would add all the files generated by PyInstaller
#  to this file.
#
#  If you do instead wish to deploy a folder, you can ignore the
#  folder at the root of your project here.
#
#  Note: PyInstaller will create a folder with the same name as your
#  script's basename. To ignore this folder, you can use the
#  following pattern:
#
#  <script_name>/
#
*.spec


